l cells in the 2D rectangle from A1 to C3\n\nFor resolving a block range:\n```typescript\nfunction resolveRange(start: string, end: string): string[] {\n  const startCol = columnToNumber(getColumn(start));\n  const startRow = getRow(start);\n  const endCol = columnToNumber(getColumn(end));\n  const endRow = getRow(end);\n  \n  const cells: string[] = [];\n  for (let col = Math.min(startCol, endCol); col <= Math.max(startCol, endCol); col++) {\n    for (let row = Math.min(startRow, endRow); row <= Math.max(startRow, endRow); row++) {\n      cells.push(numberToColumn(col) + row);\n    }\n  }\n  return cells;\n}\n```\n\nFor a column range: startCol = endCol, so we iterate rows.\nFor a row range: startRow = endRow, so we iterate columns.\nFor a block range: both vary.\n\nThis naturally handles all three cases. ✓\n\nAlright, let me write the code!\n\nLet me also think about an edge case: what happens when a cell formula references a cell that has an error? For example, if A1 contains a formula that throws (division by zero?), the evaluator could catch the error and... hmm, the spec doesn't mention error values. Let me just let errors propagate as exceptions for now.\n\nOK, let me start coding. I'll create task items and work through them.","signature":"6eb125e8-c2f7-4902-991d-018588dfca9f"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":640,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":22016,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b44ad63f-2e77-4176-9769-43b8093ff773","uuid":"8323df48-8059-4c98-868f-9d1eadf3cb23"}
